irection with momentum and rubber-band bounds. The draggable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card responds to touch input via Origami’s "},{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" patch, which wires its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"output "},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card snaps back to its resting position."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Interaction_DragView","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Interaction_DragView","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Interaction_DragView","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/navigationDocument(_:preview:)-6v0j4":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/navigationDocument(_:preview:)-6v0j4","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/navigationdocument(_:preview:)-6v0j4","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"navigationDocument"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"D"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"D"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"preview"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI12SharePreviewV","text":"SharePreview"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5NeverO","text":"Never"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5NeverO","text":"Never"},{"kind":"text","text":">) -> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI4ViewP","text":"View"}],"title":"navigationDocument(_:preview:)","type":"topic","abstract":[]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"url":"\/documentation\/swami","title":"Swami","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"}}}